    "scope": "Container cgroup v2 totals include the JVM and Python, including any JVM startup before Python entry; deltas cover observed intervals only. Process CPU/IO deltas never bridge a changed PID/start-tick generation. Process CPU counters have 1/SC_CLK_TCK-second resolution: interval utilization requires at least 10 ticks of elapsed time, and whole-run utilization requires the same minimum total observed duration. Short intervals are counted and excluded only from utilization peaks/interval summaries, never CPU core-seconds or raw counters. Cgroup CPU has microsecond counter resolution and uses its observed intervals without the process tick threshold. Cgroup charged memory includes page cache; Python/JVM RSS and lifetime peaks are separate and must not be summed. Memory means are sample means. /tmp and /results statvfs values are shared-filesystem capacity/free space, not per-job disk allocation. Block IO counters are container/VM accounting, not physical-drive latency; devices are separate and stacked devices must not be summed; Python/JVM rchar/wchar are syscall bytes, not disk bytes. Missing counters/devices remain unavailable, not zero."
